Changelog: 22-11-2026 11:44:56

Added. The row beside the title has a new state, Steam. Its dot is green while Steam runs and is signed in, and red when
it is not, because a game in Steam starts only then. The app looks again every few seconds. The states now show their
names alone, Installed, Controller and Steam, and the dot's color shows the state. Each tooltip opens with the state in
full, such as Not installed or No controller. The wiki describes the row. test_main_window.py tests the Steam state and
follows the new order.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 12:04:44

Release 1.7.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 19:26:09

Release 1.6.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 18:49:20

Added. The window's new order (owner, 20-11-2026: shadPS4 Manager's design in every manager). The header's pills are
the Xenia version, Xenia Install, Xenia Uninstall and Refresh. The row under them is Games Uninstall and Available
in Steam. Games Uninstall is new: it is what the Remove game… button under the table did, and that button went. The
Your games box went. Under the pills are two columns: the two state lines, each name with a colon (Xenia:, Game
folder:), and beside them Installed version:, the Xenia version in use. The tabs are Your games, Start game, Memory
cards, Settings, View logs (it was Log) and Clear logs.

Added. A check for a game that is in Steam more than once. The app says which games and how often, the game's In
Steam box says it in its tooltip, and Update Steam lights and leaves one shortcut of each, with the latest play
time; its question says how many double shortcuts go.

Fixed. The chosen row of a table is 30 % blue, with the theme's text color: filled with the header's blue, a chosen
first row could hardly be told from the header above it.

Fixed. Start game with Steam closed started Steam and never the game, while the line said "Steam starts" (seen in
shadPS4 Manager on the board, 20-11-2026). The app now starts Steam first, waits until it takes commands, then gives
it the game's address, again when the game does not come up (core's play). The line says the game runs only once
Xenia does, and says when Steam did not start it. While Xenia runs already, Start game starts no second one.

Fixed. A shortcut whose fields Steam wrote in lower case (exe, launchoptions) was not recognized as the app's, so
Update Steam added the game a second time. They are read whatever their case now.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 13:11:18

Release 1.5.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 03:39:29

Added. The version manager (owner, 20-11-2026: as shadPS4's own launcher has one; core's builds). The version box in
the header is a pill: its menu lists the Xenia builds installed and puts another in use, and Manage versions… opens
the version manager, which downloads the Canary builds from GitHub, checked against the SHA-256 GitHub publishes, adds
a custom AppImage, puts a build in use and deletes one. Builds stay side by side: Install no longer deletes the
others, and puts the build this version was tried with back in use, without a download when it is still there.
Uninstall removes every build. A build other than the tested one is said to be not tried on the board.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 02:49:29

Release 1.4.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 02:18:33

Added. The app installs Xenia Canary build 54386cb (19-11-2026; was 838850f; action list, 20-11-2026): emulator.py
pins its commit, release date, the SHA-256 GitHub publishes for its AppImage (fbd24aa7…e4b6) and its size, now
about 16 MB (was 18: Xenia moved from SDL2 to SDL3 on 12-11-2026, for sound and controllers). Checked in Xenia's
source between the two builds (152 changes): no setting the app writes changed. Xenia removed its ALSA sound
system and sets a config that names it back to Automatic; the app offers Automatic and SDL only, as before.

Changelog: 19-11-2026 22:33:16

Release 1.3.1.

Changelog: 19-11-2026 22:12:37

Fixed. The message about a newer build says it comes once it has been tried on the board, not the console (owner, 19-11-2026: board everywhere).

Changelog: 18-11-2026 04:15:16

Release 1.3.0.

Changelog: 18-11-2026 03:30:14

Added. The controller's state beside the title, as the other managers show it: Controller connected, or No
controller when none is, looked at again every few seconds.

Changelog: 18-11-2026 03:27:50

Added. The managers' new design, as the other managers': a Memory cards tab with the saved games Xenia keeps,
each under its game's title (export to a .zip, import, delete). Clear logs, a tab beside Log that is a button,
empties the app's log file and the Log tab and removes the older log files. Start game stands beside Your games.
The six tabs share the window's whole width and are pills as the ones above them. Under the header's pills only
the links to Xenia's release notes and the wiki are left, in the type of a pill's caption; the introduction went.
Xenia's state is one line. Under the games an info symbol stands in for the line of text about Steam. The window
opens 900 wide (it was 980), which is its narrowest, and 606 high (it was 800); the Settings tab scrolls when it
is higher than the window. There is no Play time pill: Xenia counts none.

